\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 README: The 1/3 Country Project (NCVS 2023)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf2 Research Abstract: Measuring the National Safety Gap\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa320\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 This study utilizes a high-fidelity analytical pipeline to examine the "Safety Gap" between disparate economic geographies in the United States, colloquially referred to as the "Three Countries" (Bottom, Middle, and Top income terciles). By implementing a 3-way relational join of the 2023 National Crime Victimization Survey (NCVS) microdata, this research moves beyond traditional incident-frequency reporting to establish true Weighted Prevalence Rates.\
Anchored on a robust population universe of 149,804 valid observations, the analysis incorporates non-victimized individuals to create a statistically accurate national denominator. This methodology enables the calculation of Risk Ratios, quantifying the specific probability of victimization and the nature of police interaction as a function of household income. The findings provide a critical empirical lens on the socioeconomic stratification of public safety in the United States.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 1. Project Overview\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The 1/3 Country Project segments the U.S. population into three income-based "Countries" to measure the lived experience of safety.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The project aims to visualize how the "National Myth" of uniform safety disintegrates when viewed through the lens of economic terciles.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The analysis focuses on three key metrics: Violent Victimization, Property Victimization, and Police Interaction.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

